@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] workspace-isolation
Every filesystem operation MUST derive its workspace and grants from its authenticated session.
Neither matching grants nor knowledge of an object ID MUST permit cross-workspace access.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] live-authorization
Every read MUST authorize and return data from one consistent SlateDB snapshot. Every mutation MUST
validate current authorization through publication. Effective grants are explicit grants on the
object and its ancestors. Workspace keys alone authorize grant administration and session creation;
the server key alone authorizes workspace creation. Sessions MUST reject more than 512 distinct grants.
Expired, closed, and previous-process sessions MUST fail authorization.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] private-projections
Root and /shared MUST expose only authorized entries. Shared entries MUST use basename--object-id.
Synthetic entries MUST NOT be mutated. Inode parents MUST follow the visible projection, never expose
hidden canonical ancestry. Missing and inaccessible objects MUST produce indistinguishable errors.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:backend] atomic-filesystem-mutations
Each mutation MUST atomically publish its blocks, object records, child entries, and both explicit
grant indexes in one SlateDB batch. Reads MUST NOT observe a partial mutation. Shrink followed by
extension MUST return zeros for removed bytes. Renames MUST preserve object identity and reject cycles.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:concurrency] compare-and-publish
A mutation MUST compare expected versions under synchronization covering authorization and publication.
A mismatch MUST publish nothing. Each changed object MUST advance its version once. Unrelated files
MUST have independent versions. No automatic retry may replace a rejected expected version.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:performance;backend] memory-acknowledgement
Success MUST await SlateDB memory publication but MUST NOT await remote durability. Fsync MUST wait
for preceding client writes and propagate errors without flushing SlateDB. SlateDB's internal WAL
MUST remain enabled. Recovery MUST retain complete batches only; losing recent acknowledgements is
allowed. An application WAL, overlay, or persistence worker MUST NOT be introduced.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:backend;performance] bounded-slate-storage
All file contents MUST use SlateDB keys with at most 65536 bytes per block. No separate GCS blobs.
Requests, batches, caches, and retained handles MUST be bounded; large files MUST NOT require buffers
proportional to file size. Server cache budgets MUST be shared across workspaces and configurable.
Every restart MUST discard local caches and recover only from remote durable state.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;error-handling] transport-boundary
Credentials MUST appear only in RPC metadata or protected credential files, never URLs or logs.
Errors MUST NOT expose hidden names, grants, or backend details. FUSE MUST use direct I/O, no kernel
writeback, no data cache, and zero metadata TTL. Version conflicts MUST reach the caller as EAGAIN;
ambiguous writes MUST return an error and MUST NOT be automatically replayed.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:rust] fallible-rust
Rust code MUST propagate or explicitly handle fallible operations; unwrap() and expect() are forbidden.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;backend] gcs-adc-identity
GCS authentication MUST use GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS, local application-default credentials,
or the attached service identity. Unrelated SERVICE_ACCOUNT configuration MUST NOT override ADC.
